body:
Owner request of 2026-09-29, relayed by the orchestrator (journal, process/decision, 08:29Z):

> Put the experiments, the observations and the suggestions from the Fable review into separate pages …, so I can find them on the site as a documented history of the project's evolution and of the current status. Break that page into topic-oriented parts that document what I suggested, what you analysed, and what happened in each subject. It should be living documentation, valid over time … an index to all the status material, which keeps accumulating. Entries are not replaced at each project phase.

Clarifications that followed:
- newest first everywhere, like a stack;
- document everything tried, run and obtained, including failed and restarted attempts;
- rename `/project` to `/experiments` (old paths redirect) and show ALL major tasks, not only training experiments;
- every task page separates the **Owner** side from the **Agents / analysis** side.
